From: Local <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] FIX: window: Activate, raise and unrestricted resize is unrestricted

performMouseCommand() made a resize unrestricted only for MouseUnrestrictedResize, not for
MouseActivateRaiseAndUnrestrictedResize - the default of Meta + right drag - unlike the move
branch, which checks both. With 6.8's confinement of xdg-toplevel geometry changes (18b044c)
the default Meta + right resize of a window partly above the screen pulled it back down
(2026-10-09, the user's report; research/kwin-resize-jump-2026-10-09.md).
---
diff --git a/src/window.cpp b/src/window.cpp
index e01ccbe..d9c82e1 100644
--- a/src/window.cpp
+++ b/src/window.cpp
@@ -2201,7 +2201,8 @@ bool Window::performMousePressCommand(Options::MouseCommand cmd, const QPointF &
             gravity = (x < width() / 2) ? Gravity::Left : Gravity::Right;
         }
         setInteractiveMoveResizeGravity(gravity);
-        setUnrestrictedInteractiveMoveResize((cmd == Options::MouseUnrestrictedResize));
+        setUnrestrictedInteractiveMoveResize((cmd == Options::MouseActivateRaiseAndUnrestrictedResize
+                                              || cmd == Options::MouseUnrestrictedResize));
         if (!startInteractiveMoveResize()) {
             setInteractiveMoveResizePointerButtonDown(false);
         }
